  "pack": "3.3.4",
  "description": "Wild food blocks a player can harvest early (berry bushes, herbs, HarvestCraft gardens, mushrooms) and nearby plant hazards, for forageFood, forageSources and forageHazard. Hand-written from the bytecode of the pinned pack jars (Rustic 1.1.7, Biomes O' Plenty 7.0.1.2445, Pam's HarvestCraft zg, Dropt 1.19.4 with athenaeum 1.19.6, CraftTweaker 4.1.20.700), read with javap only, and from the pack's scripts and configs; excerpts and copies in packages/rotn-data/test/fixtures/forage-food-3.3.4/. confidence \"verified\" = read from that bytecode, script and config; nothing here was watched in a run. Food values are not copied here: forageFood attaches foodValues and avoidFood from food-values.json.",
  "confidence": "verified",
  "summary": "Best early forage: Rustic wildberry bushes (rustic:wildberry_bush). Right-click one with berries (meta 1): 1 wildberries, the bush stays and regrows berries (about 24 min in daylight). Do not break it: Dropt replaces its drops, mostly sticks. Hawthorn (biomesoplenty:plant_0 meta 5, BoP's berry bush): never right-click it (the pack's script poisons and hits the player for 4), break it instead for 1 berry. Wild Rustic herbs (ginseng, marsh mallow, core root) spawn grown: break for 1-3. HarvestCraft gardens: break without sneaking for 2 different crops. Mushrooms are not food raw (smelt them). Avoid touching poison ivy (biomesoplenty:plant_0 meta 4) and thorns/tiny cacti (plant_1 meta 2, 6) without boots and leggings. None of these foods is poisonous to eat except cloudsbluff (avoidFood); wildberries give only 1 hunger here.",
