  "evidence": [
    "Wildberry right-click: Rustic BlockBerryBush.onBlockActivated (func_180639_a): when BERRIES is true and the held stack is not bone meal (Items.DYE meta 15), it sets BERRIES false (setBlockState, flag 3), makes new ItemStack(getBerries()) (count 1), gives it with addItemStackToInventory or else spawnAsEntity on the player's side, and returns true; with BERRIES false it returns false. ModBlocks$3 (the dump's class for rustic:wildberry_bush) getBerries = ModItems.WILDBERRIES",
    "Wildberry states: getMetaFromState (func_176201_c) is 1 for BERRIES true, else 0; the dump's states agree (meta 0 berries=false, meta 1 berries=true). Constructor: Material.PLANTS, hardness 0.2",
    "Wildberry regrowth: updateTick (func_180650_b): when getLightFromNeighbors(pos.up()) >= 9 and BERRIES is false, nextInt((int) (40.0 / 2.0) + 1) == 0 (1 in 21, through ForgeHooks.onCropsGrowPre) sets BERRIES true. With the default randomTickSpeed 3 a block gets a random tick about every 4096 / 3 = 1365 game ticks, so about 21 x 1365 ticks = 24 minutes on average",
    "Wildberry touch: getCollisionBoundingBox (func_180646_a) returns NULL_AABB (no collision); onEntityCollidedWithBlock multiplies motionX and motionZ by 0.6. No damage",
    "Wildberry spawn: WorldGenWildberries.biomeBlacklist (static init) COLD, SNOWY, SANDY, SAVANNA, MESA, MUSHROOM, NETHER, END, DEAD, WASTELAND; generateBush sets BERRIES to Random.nextBoolean(); config/rustic.cfg 'Wildberry Generation Chance'=0.05, 'Max Wildberry Generation Attempts'=4",
    "Dropt rules (scripts/dropt.zs, loaded by CraftTweaker): athenaeum RecipeItemParser.parse sets meta 0 unless there is a third segment ('*' = 32767), and Dropt's BlockMatchEntry.matches compares Block.getMetaFromState with it (32767 = any meta). So \"rustic:wildberry_bush\" (list Berry_Good) matches only meta 0 and \"rustic:wildberry_bush:1\" only meta 1. RuleLocator.matchRules keeps the first matching rule unless it sets fallthrough (Rule default false). Rule defaults: replaceStrategy REPLACE_ALL, dropStrategy REPEAT, dropCount 1; RuleDropItem quantity 1. DropModifier.modifyDrops adds every force() drop, puts the other drops that RuleDropSelector.isValidCandidate allows (silktouch REQUIRED needs Silk Touch, EXCLUDED forbids it; fortune level) into a WeightedPicker with weight + fortune modifier, picks dropCount times, and with REPLACE_ALL_IF_SELECTED clears the block's own drops when it picked something. No other rule in scripts/dropt.zs or the pack's other Dropt scripts (dropt_loose_materials.zs, dropt_magicite.zs, future-mc.zs, contentweaker/contentTweaker_Dropt.zs) names the wildberry bush; Pyrotech's Dropt plugin categories (config/pyrotech/plugin.Dropt.cfg) are all off",
    "Hawthorn: biomesoplenty:plant_0 meta 5 is BOPPlants.BERRYBUSH (enum order; the dump's state variant=berrybush). BlockBOPPlant.onBlockActivated: for BERRYBUSH (BlockBOPPlant$2 switch index 5) it sets the BUSH variant (plant_0 meta 2), spawns an EntityItem of BOPItems.berries and calls onCollideWithPlayer (not for a FakePlayer), and returns true. getDrops: BERRYBUSH gives one BOPItems.berries. ModItems: berries = new ItemBOPFood(1, 0.1, 8); ItemBOPFood's constructor and methods set no potion effect",
    "Hawthorn harm: scripts/events.zs line 201 events.onPlayerInteractBlock. CraftTweaker's MTEventManager.onPlayerInteractBlock delegates to onPlayerRightClickBlock, which CommonEventHandler.onPlayerRightClickBlockEvent (Forge PlayerInteractEvent$RightClickBlock) publishes. Lines 221-226: for biomesoplenty:plant_0 meta 5, addPotionEffect(poison, 40 ticks, amplifier 1) and attackEntityFrom(CACTUS, 4), then return without event.cancel(). The pack's scripts have no other block right-click or left-click handler for these blocks (events.zs line 871 only checks multiblockmobs:soul_chassis; no other .zs file hooks block interaction), so breaking the bush (a left click) is safe; BoP berry bushes have no collision effect",
    "Plant hazards: BlockBOPPlant.onEntityCollidedWithBlock (func_180634_a): POISONIVY (switch index 3) gives a player Poison for 100 ticks, and THORN and TINYCACTUS (16, 22) deal 1 CACTUS damage, unless both armorInventory slots 0 (feet) and 1 (legs) are filled. The dump: plant_0 meta 4 poisonivy; plant_1 meta 2 thorn, meta 6 tinycactus",
    "Rustic herbs: BlockHerbBase.getDrops: BlockBush.getDrops (getItemDropped = getHerb: 1) plus, at getMaxAge 3, 2 + fortune rolls that each add the herb when nextInt(2 x 3) <= age (4 in 6). WorldGenSurfaceHerbs places them at AGE 3. There is no onBlockActivated, so breaking is the harvest. Herbs$4/$6/$8/$10.getHerb = CLOUDSBLUFF/CORE_ROOT/GINSENG/MARSH_MALLOW (ItemHerbEdible, registered under the block's registry name, no potion effect in its constructor or methods); the dump's classes map those to rustic:cloudsbluff, core_root, ginseng, marsh_mallow. Herbs.getRandomHerbForBiome picks by BiomeDictionary type (where). config/rustic.cfg 'Herb Generation Chance'=0.125, 'Max Herb Generation Attempts'=8",
    "HarvestCraft gardens: BlockBaseGarden.getDrops shuffles the garden's drop list and adds the first min(gardendropAmount, size) items, one each; config/harvestcraft.cfg gardendropAmount=2, the six enable*gardenGeneration=true, enablegardenSpread=false, and the drops lists (RotN edited them). harvestBlock (func_180657_a) drops getSilkTouchDrop (the garden itself) when the player is sneaking (func_70093_af) or uses Silk Touch, else the normal drops",
    "Mushrooms: the dump's minecraft:brown_mushroom and red_mushroom (vanilla BlockMushroom) drop themselves; foodValues gives null for both (not food). smeltingOf: brown -> betterwithaddons:food_mushroom_baked, red -> betterwithaddons:food_amanita_baked. Better With Addons 0.51 is in the pinned zip (mods/Better With Addons-0.51.jar, SHA-256 fc06cccbd05b6f49b72f3dff5f68d594782df648ec1550439411856e06785f0e): ModItems registers food_mushroom_baked as ItemFood(3, 0.2) with no effect, and food_amanita_baked as ItemFood(3, 0.2).setPotionEffect(Poison, 100 ticks, amplifier 0, chance 1.0), so the baked amanita always poisons for 5 s; avoidFood lists it and forageFood's cook[].avoid carries it (lead's #423 review)"
